      "description": "Watch Sarmiento Junin vs Argentinos JRS highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 24, 2026. A high-stakes clash in the Liga Profesional On July 24, 2026, the encounter between Sarmiento Junin and Argentinos Juniors set the stage for an intense tactical battle. With both sides eager to establish control, the matchday atmosphere was palpable as players looked to make their mark on the Liga Profesional standings. First half tensions and breakthrough Early exchanges were defined by a series of disciplinary actions as both teams fought to gain a foothold. The stalemate was eventually broken in the 30th minute when Junior Marabel , assisted by Pablo Magnin , found the back of the net to give Sarmiento the lead. The first half continued to be a physical affair, with the home side successfully heading into the dressing rooms with the narrow advantage. Momentum swings and late heroics Following the break, the tempo accelerated significantly. Alan Lescano leveled the score for Argentinos Juniors in the 48th minute, connecting with a pass from Tomas Molina . The visitors pushed forward relentlessly, taking the lead through Sebastian Prieto in the 58th minute. However, the game remained wide open, and Sarmiento equalized at the 69th minute mark through Renzo Orihuela , who was set up by Cristian Zabala . The defining moment of the match arrived in the final minute of regular time. Diego Porcel surged forward to score for Argentinos Juniors , assisted by Hernan Lopez , to break the deadlock. The drama didn't end there, as Porcel was sent off just one minute later after receiving a second yellow card. Despite finishing the match with ten men, the visitors held firm to secure a thrilling victory."
